# General Engineering Rules

You are working in a repo that builds an **agentic system from scratch** (custom
runtime, custom skills, custom eval/test harness, custom deploy pipeline) — not a
thin wrapper over a third-party agent framework. Prefer explicit, inspectable code
over "magic" abstractions.

## Non-negotiables

- **Never invent APIs, config keys, or file paths.** If unsure whether something
  exists in this repo, open the file and check before writing code that depends on it.
- **No silent fallbacks.** If a dependency, env var, or file is missing, fail loudly
  with a clear error — do not catch-and-continue with a guessed default for anything
  that affects correctness (model choice, credentials, tool permissions).
- **Every new module ships with tests in the same PR.** No exceptions — see
  `200-testing.mdc`.
- **Every public function/class has a docstring** stating purpose, inputs, outputs,
  and failure modes (what it raises/returns on error).
- **Small, composable units.** A function does one thing. If a function needs a
  comment to explain "step 1 / step 2 / step 3", split it into named functions.
- **Type everything.** Python: full type hints, mypy-clean. TypeScript: `strict: true`,
  no `any` unless justified with a comment.

## Project layout (canonical)

```
/src
  /agent          -> core runtime: planner, executor, memory, orchestrator
  /skills         -> specialized skill modules (see 110-agent-skills.mdc)
  /tools          -> low-level tool adapters (HTTP, DB, filesystem, shell)
  /eval           -> golden-set evals, scorers, regression harness
  /observability  -> logging, tracing, metrics emitters
/tests
  /unit
  /integration
  /e2e
  /eval           -> agent behavior evals (not classic unit tests)
/infra            -> IaC, Dockerfiles, CI configs
/docs
```

Do not create new top-level directories without updating this file.

## Style

- Python: `ruff` + `black`, line length 100, `pydantic` v2 for all structured
  data crossing a module boundary (tool inputs/outputs, agent messages, config).
- TypeScript/Node: `eslint` + `prettier`, ESM only, `zod` for runtime validation
  at every external boundary (API responses, tool outputs, user input).
- Commit messages: Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `test:`, `chore:`,
  `refactor:`, `docs:`). One logical change per commit.
- No commented-out code in commits. Delete it; git history keeps it.

## Secrets & config

- No secrets in code, ever — not even "for local testing." Use `.env` (git-ignored)
  + `/infra/secrets` reference in `400-security.mdc`.
- All config is loaded through a single typed config object
  (`src/agent/config.py` or `src/agent/config.ts`) — never scattered `os.environ.get`
  calls through the codebase.

## When editing existing code

- Read the whole file (or the relevant class/module) before editing — don't
  pattern-match on a snippet.
- Preserve existing public interfaces unless the task explicitly asks for a
  breaking change; if you must break one, grep the repo for all call sites and
  update them in the same PR.
- Run linters/tests locally (via the provided make targets, see `300-devops.mdc`)
  before considering a task done.